diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index ad2447b978fd25271c914210faf5aef16c9b690b..e66127a0fa4afe2c7f675006473a7f59e28a78df 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -134,6 +134,17 @@ share one daemon through a private Unix socket, with independent timezone views.
 without replacing or stopping older daemons; each build has its own scanning and memory cost.
 No HTTP server, TCP listener, Python runtime or sudo is required.
 
+Subscription quota is separate from log-derived token usage. In Settings → Subscription,
+select the local or enabled SSH host's Codex / OpenCode Go source, or use All sources
+to include enabled remote hosts automatically. Sign in with the provider on that
+host first; no local login is needed for remote-only quota. The collector reads
+the remote login and queries the supplier there; credentials are never downloaded
+to the desktop. Quota cards and the quota floating panel identify each host and
+keep its account limits separate. The desktop network switch disables supplier
+quota requests without stopping ordinary SSH metrics. A disconnected host retains
+its last successful quota as stale, not measured zero. This queue increment is
+unreleased and requires a collector built with remote quota support.
+
 Optional mobile live-activity authorization is separate: after the user creates an activity in the foreground, an
 activity-scoped lease can authorize the daemon to send only minimal current metrics over verified HTTPS to
 `https://agent-speed.yooztech.com`. Confirmed authorization can survive the last SSH exit, subject to host logout policy,
