 ## 1. Common rules
 
@@ -398,3 +401,36 @@ not the target host. Read access does not renew publisher authority, and removin
 pushes while a separately consented publisher lease continues storing bounded statistics until expiry.
 Local development checks and an unpublished ELF are not proof of production deployment or Apple delivery.
 
+## 10. Subscription quota on local and remote hosts
+
+Subscription settings select local and enabled SSH-host Codex/OpenCode Go sources.
+Selecting a remote source authorizes the collector to read that host's existing
+provider login without modifying it and to query the supplier on that host when
+network access is enabled. No login or provider secret is downloaded to the
+desktop. The existing SSH connection carries correlated requests and structured
+quota observations only, not raw supplier responses. The quota command is
+independent of token sampling, mobile leases, Widget feeds and desktop reporting;
+none of those authorizes quota polling on its own.
+
