+Codenotch reference. An OAuth 401 may require the authenticated Console
+`/api/user` probe to distinguish missing Go entitlement from sign-out. Supplier
+requests include the provider's bearer credential and its required account or
+organization header, only on the credential-owning host. Redirects must not
+forward credentials to another destination. Authorization headers, credentials
+and raw response bodies never enter logs, desktop messages or quota caches.
+
+The network switch disables automatic and manual supplier refreshes, including
+remote refreshes, without closing ordinary SSH monitoring. Cache-only quota
+requests make no supplier HTTP request. Source exclusion, host disable/removal
+and consent revocation invalidate pending desktop results. A disconnected
+desktop leaves no autonomous quota-polling lease: quota work is request-driven.
+Automatic refresh follows the existing five-minute quota cadence; manual
+refresh respects persisted provider backoff, Retry-After and Codex request floors.
+Unknown values remain null, failed observations retain an original timestamp
+only when shown as stale, and independent account limits are never summed.
+See [`QUOTA.md`](QUOTA.md) for provider parsing, cache isolation and wire details.
+
